tment because it costs quite a lot  to restore something like this  the medieval holiday model is often  worth the investment  in 2007 the italian village castelfalfi  lay in ruins only five people lived in  the small town just west of florence  german travel company tui bought the 11  square kilometers around the village and  invested some 250 million euros  a second hotel is just open for business  here only the facade is medieval the  interior is entirely modern  most investors buy up the village and  strip away its identity they don't care  about the villages like albert  they just turn them into tourist  villages  foreign investors think in these  categories as well  they don't care about the village like  one of the residents would  but it doesn't have to be that way  25 people now live in the village of  monte gridolfo  most local residents found work at the  hotel  these are jobs that help ensure the  future of their community  these jobs are really important to us  the more visitors come and the better  they feel the more tourism we'll have  and the more jobs for local people  everything is changing there was nothing  here before it was just a small town and  deserted now we've got life here again  so it's a very fundamental change  a vacation in the middle ages can be  just an investment  or with a little more respect it can  also be a dream come true for both  locals and tourists  well german basketball player duke  novitskiy is a superstar in the u.s but  when he comes home to germany he does  tend to slip back into his role of boy  next door in his hometown of woltzburg  which is why it's so interesting that a  new documentary will reveal something  more about his personal life the perfect  shot tells the story of his fabulous  career with the dallas mavericks and we  got a sneak preview before it hits the  theaters in september  scenes from the life of one of  basketball's greats  dirk nowitzki has been playing for  america's national basketball  association since 1998.  the man with the perfect shot is feared  by his opponents and worth millions of  dollars to his team the dallas mavericks  a german camera crew followed his life  for two years getting up close and  personal with the game and the player  the end result previewed for the media  on thursday in frankfort nowitzki  himself hasn't seen it he says he has  complete confidence in the director even  if it took him some time to warm up to  the idea  mine under asthma my first reaction was  are you kidding me  i'm actually a pretty private person  i don't have to have everything  displayed in public  and then the second thing i said was my  life is so boring  i just play a little basketball  but the prize-winning documentary maker  sebastian denhart won him over he had  already made films on the boxer brothers  vitali and vladimir klitschko  we wanted to reduce it to a minimum  so we didn't have five six seven people  standing around in the shot  that's what we did  we wanted to make it look like the  camera wasn't there and i think we did  it  dirk novitskiy's discoverer and mentor  holger schwintner plays a leading role  in the film and in the star's life his  unorthodox methods have helped make  novitskiy a world-class player from  vancouver it's crazy the ideas he has  when we started out i was 15 or 16. i  couldn't really figure out what he  wanted from me  among the film's strong points are the  friends and family who add their own  perspectives dirk nowitzki's wife  jessica  they sort of have this  relationship where they understand each  other without even talking to each other  there's many times when i've asked dirk  what is you know  for example when is holger arriving or  when is hogger leaving and he has no  idea  and uh  i don't know maybe they have their own  language  himself initiated the documentary  without even discussing it with nowitzki  in advance  when i was playing basketball nobody  cared you could send a postcard from  italy and it would arrive nine months  later now you get the latest information  in one second  i think film is an appropriate medium to  document his career and i hope it'll be  interesting in 10 years he'll have  something to show his kids  it's a film about the fascination of  basketball and a teenager who left  germany for the united states to play  with the world's best  the film brings together superstars of  basketball old school mates and many  others to define the dirk nowitzki  phenomenon  what i liked most was that it's a really  authentic portrait of dirk  they only had a few days of shooting it  wasn't like they followed us around for  two years but they really captured the  spirit of him as a person  now novitskiy intends to watch the film  for the first time with his fans at the  world premiere on september 16th in  cologne  and with that it is time for us to sign  off so until we meet again all the best  from us here in summertime berlin and  bye-bye  you
 

